    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Dog Sit Home, on rue d'Antibes in Cannes, is first and foremost a professional grooming salon and daycare, run by Johnny Vanderstraeten (SIRET confirmed). It also offers a self-service wash option — but keep in mind this is not a pure automated station like you might find elsewhere in the department, for example in Nice.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The salon's services include hair removal, massage and hydrotherapy. A "4 baths + full grooming" package at €100 a month is mentioned, but the price for the self-service wash alone is not known separately. The address and the manager's identity are confirmed by the official business register, PagesJaunes and Mappy, which gives good reliability on these points; the exact nature of the "dogwash" offer (self-service added to a salon, rather than a standalone station) is more nuanced and worth checking on site.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if you're only after a quick, affordable wash with no appointment, call ahead to confirm that the self-service option is actually accessible without going through the grooming package.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Rue d'Antibes is one of the main shopping streets in central Cannes, a few minutes from the Croisette.</p>
